          %title
          %p
            This is a sub-entry for
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gerbe"} gerbe
          %p For related entries see
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundle+gerbe"} bundle gerbe
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gerbe+%28general+idea%29"} gerbe (general idea)
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            (The definitions of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stack"} stack
            are elsewhere in the nLab but we will have to review them briefly. There is also
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/motivation+for+sheaves%2C+cohomology+and+higher+stacks"} motivation for sheaves, cohomology and higher stacks
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            rather than in the more general setting of a topos.)
          %p
            Naively a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/family+of+sets"} family of sets
            indexed ‘continuously’ by the points of a space
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaf
            satisfying a ‘gluing condition’ (which is the version of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent"} descent
            in one of its simplest cases), or to an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/etale+space"} étalé space
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
          %p
            An important class of sheaves are the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torsor"} torsors
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            be a sheaf of groups on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Tors
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mo ;
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Tors(B;G)
            of
            = succeed "-torsors" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            is a groupoid. The notion of
            = succeed "-torsor" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            is an open set of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            to a sheaf on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            using the restricted
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Tors
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo ;
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Tors(U;G)
            for the corresponding groupoid. If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            is another open set contained in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Tors
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo ;
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Tors(U;G)
            to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Tors
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ;
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Tors(V;G)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
          %p
            The assignment of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Tors
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Tors(G)_U
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            only gives a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudofunctor"} pseudofunctor
            not a functor from the category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Open
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Open(B)^{op}
            to the category of groupoids. It thus corresponds to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+fibration"} Grothendieck fibration
            or
            %strong fibred category
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Open
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Open(B)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stack"} stack
            of groupoids. (Roughly ‘morphisms glue, objects glue up to isomorphism’. For enlightenment note that there are almost presheaves of objects and of morphisms in this ‘pseudo’ presheaf.) This stack will be called
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒯
                    %mi ors
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T}ors(G)
          %p
            There is a
            %strong stackcompletion
            functor from fibred categories to stacks. If we take the sheaf of groups
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi BG
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} BG
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Open
