            = succeed "-bundle.)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %p
            Groups ‘are’ groupoids with a single object, but groupoids are not ‘groups with many objects’ (although that is a nice phrase to use when introducing them). A groupoid need not have any objects … if it is empty! Of course, we think of the vertex groups of a groupoid, but, if the groupoid is not connected, there may be many different non-isomorphic ones. So a group
            %em is
            a very special type of groupoid.
          %p Similarly, the term ‘gerbe’ refers to a special sort of stack of groupoids.
          .standout
            %p A gerbe is to a general stack what, up to equivalence, a group is to a general groupoid. It is non-empty and connected.
          .query
            %p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Roberts"}> David Roberts
              \: This is reflected in the fact that the fibres of bundle gerbes (either abelian or
              = succeed "-bundles" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              = succeed "?" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gerbe+%28general+idea%29"} gerbe (general idea)
          %p To make this precise we use some additional notions:
          %p
            We will have a pseudofunctor
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %mi Open
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %mi Grpd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : Open(B)^{op}\to Grpd
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                A stack of groupoids,
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                is
                %em locally non-empty
                if there is an open covering
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒰
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{U}
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                for which each groupoid
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(U)
                is non-empty, for
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi 𝒰
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \in \mathcal{U}
            %li
              %p
                A stack of groupoids,
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                is said to be
                %em locally connected
                if for each open
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                there is an open covering
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒰
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{U}
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                such that all elements in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(U)
                become connected in all
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
